WEBVTT

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:06.240
The festival of dreams
to crown the strongest Pokémon Trainer...

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.530
The Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.620
The eight mighty trainers
aiming for the summit...

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.330
...have begun battling.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.750
And the semifinals are today.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:21.670
The first match will be
Dande versus Carne.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:25.000
The second match will be
Shirona versus Satoshi.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:28.630
Fierce battles are in store
as they vie for a spot in the finals.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:36.100
Near Shoot Stadium
stands Hotel Lond Rose.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:40.020
This is where staff and participants
of the Masters Tournament are staying.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:59.290
Hey...

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.460
Go!

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.130
Have you been up all night?

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:09.970
Yeah!

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:14.180
Project Mew sent me
all this material!

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:19.270
So I’ve been organizing the info
in my own way.

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:21.640
Whoa... That’s amazing!

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:26.570
Now I’ll be ready,
no matter when they call me!

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:28.820
Do your best,
and go find Mew!

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:29.530
Right!

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.450
I’m counting on you
to get through the semifinals, too!

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:33.490
Yeah!

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:33.030
All right, that’s enough!
You’re all looking nice and sharp!

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:34.320
That’s the spirit!

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:36.700
Naturally, they’re all fired up.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.750
Satoshi! Kairyu!

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:51.710
Ms. Shirona!

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.050
Sorry for disturbing you...

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:58.220
It’s okay! Don’t worry about it.

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:02.930
By the looks of it, I assume you were
doing final preparations before our match?

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:05.100
Yeah.
You too, Ms. Shirona?

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.310
Yes.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:09.900
All right, try flying now.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:25.040
Okay, Gaburias!

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:32.630
Are you... massaging her?

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:37.050
Yes. It’s our pre-match routine.

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:42.680
It helps balance out her muscles,
aiding her maneuverability.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.390
That must feel great!

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:47.890
You’re incredible, Ms. Shirona!

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:50.560
Okay, one more try!

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:56.070
No kidding!
She’s faster now!

00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:57.360
It helps <i>that</i> much?

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:05.700
So sharp!

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.540
Yep, you’re looking good.

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:11.290
Cool! So many Pokémon!

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:13.330
Toria! Stop!

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:15.420
It’s all good.
Come on over.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:17.340
Do you like Pokémon?

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:18.380
Sure do!

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:19.720
Ah! A Pikachu!

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:23.800
It’s okay, you can touch him.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:27.770
So cute!

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:35.270
This Pokémon’s a Kairyu, right?!
Look at how big it is!

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:36.860
You can touch them, too!

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:39.490
Th-Thank you...

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:42.490
I’m Vic.
That’s my little sister, Toria.

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:44.280
I’m Satoshi!

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:46.240
And I’m Go!

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:49.700
Shirona.
Nice to meet you.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:53.880
You’re in the Masters Eight!
I’ve seen all your battles!

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:55.380
Oh! Thank you!

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:57.000
Who are you cheering for?

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:00.380
Well, I... I’m a fan of Mr. Dande,

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:02.260
but your Pikachu was cool too!

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:04.260
Huh? Pikachu?

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:07.470
10,000,000 Volts!

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:10.220
Think I can do that, too?

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:12.310
Hmm...
I wonder about that...

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:16.110
That’s a special move
only Satoshi’s Pikachu can pull off.

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:20.480
Pikachu is Satoshi’s partner.
They’ve been adventuring together for a very long time.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.610
His partner...

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:26.120
I’ve decided my first Pokémon’s
gonna be a Sarunori!

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:29.160
Sarunori? Sounds good!

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:29.870
Yeah!

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:33.410
Then I’ll evolve it into a Gorillander,
just like Mr. Dande did!

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:35.120
And get it to Kyodaimax!

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:39.380
You’ll have to evolve it
from a Sarunori to a Bachinkey first.

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:43.840
I will! I wanna pull off an awesome move
like your 10,000,000 Volts!

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:45.800
I’m sure you have it in you.

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.600
Ms. Shirona,
who was your first Pokémon?

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:51.270
Oh yeah,
I’ve never heard who it was.

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:52.390
She was.

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:56.190
We’ve traveled together
ever since she was a Fukamaru.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.520
Huh...

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:01.530
I thought it’d be more like
a Pochama, Hikozaru, or Naetle...

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:04.450
Indeed...
I hatched her from an egg.

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:05.110
An egg?!

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:08.530
Tell us, tell us!
Tell us what that was like!

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:16.790
You never know what will hatch
from a Pokémon egg, right?

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:20.590
I wondered and wondered
what it would hatch into...

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:22.800
It had my heart racing.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:28.220
Then, when I warmed it up
with all my might...

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:33.350
She hatched from it.
I was so happy.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:36.640
Wait, wait!

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:39.980
I hatched my Lucario
from an egg, too!

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:42.780
That’s right!
It was a mysterious egg.

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:43.780
Oh.

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:44.990
Mysterious?

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:48.740
It wouldn’t hatch,
no matter who warmed it up.

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:51.200
Various regions had examined it,
with no answers...

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:54.910
But the egg called out to Satoshi!

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:56.080
Wha...?!

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:57.160
Yeah!

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:59.790
I could feel his Aura,
like “Whoosh!”

00:08:00.170 --> 00:08:03.380
Lucario is called
the Aura Pokémon, isn’t it?

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:05.300
So cool!

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:07.760
Maybe he was waiting for you.

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:08.760
For me?

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:13.350
Even I had heard
about that mysterious egg.

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:16.850
So you were inside.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:21.730
Even now,
when I’m battling with Lucario,

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:26.190
it’s like “Bam!”...
I can feel my Aura growing.

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:30.110
The same thing happened
when I battled Mr. Kibana before.

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:35.200
Look after him.
I’m certain fate brought you together.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:38.330
Will I get to meet
a Pokémon by fate, too?

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:39.580
You bet!

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:43.420
I just know you’ll think
all the friends you meet were fate!

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:47.090
Thank you for telling me
all of this!

00:08:47.090 --> 00:08:49.720
Toria!
We need to get going!

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:50.430
Right!

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:52.510
Thanks, Gänger!

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:00.810
A Himenka!

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:01.900
Wait!

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:03.980
Oh... Hey! Toria!

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:08.190
Keep it up
with your battles! Bye!

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:12.620
We should be
heading out soon ourselves.

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:13.820
Yeah!

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:22.040
Now, Competitor Dande
has entered the battlefield!

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:24.340
Ooh, it’s Mr. Dande!

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:25.210
Toria!

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:27.210
Huh? That’s Vic...

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:32.340
Pikachu, Sarunori...

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:33.680
Vic!

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:34.680
What’s wrong?

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:36.100
Have you seen Toria?

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:37.100
Huh?

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:38.600
Did you get split up?

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:39.640
Yeah...

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:40.980
We’ll all look for her!

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:43.150
Don’t worry!
We’ll find her in no time!

00:09:43.150 --> 00:09:44.100
Thank you!

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:50.490
The Masters Tournament semifinals!
The first match is about to begin!

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.170
Hey! Toria!

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:12.510
Toria!

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:14.760
Say something! Toria!

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:17.010
Toria! Where are you?!

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:26.020
What?

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:35.410
Come to think of it,
I heard this earlier...

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:38.490
Doesn’t that sound like
Himenka’s singing?

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:43.790
Himenka. Flowering Pokémon.
Grass type.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:50.800
It whirls around in the wind singing a joyous song.
This delightful display has charmed many into raising it.

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:53.550
If we follow the singing,
we might find Toria!

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:54.260
Yeah!

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:56.050
Pikachu, we’re counting on you!

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:20.080
Toria!

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:21.580
Shh!

00:11:33.090 --> 00:11:34.970
It really was a Himenka.

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:37.050
Did you come here
to watch that Pokémon?

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:37.840
Yeah.

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:40.350
You have to tell me
about things like that...

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:41.350
Sorry...

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:47.600
Is it evolving?!

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:54.110
Wow!

00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:56.200
That’s Watashiraga, right?

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:56.740
Yes.

00:12:13.590 --> 00:12:14.630
It’s leaving!

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:20.430
The seeds from its cotton fluff
carry nutrients for plants and Pokémon.

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:25.310
It’s departing upon the wind
to help enrich the nature of Galar.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:27.690
Hey!

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:29.520
Bye-bye!

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:31.560
Look after yourself!

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:38.200
Oh! I forgot, Mr. Dande!

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:39.660
The battle!

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:40.910
It’s gonna start!

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:59.680
Hey, Satoshi! Look!

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:02.680
Huh? <i>What?!</i>

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:06.060
What a fierce first match!

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:10.390
Competitor Carne has already lost four Pokémon,
only having two left.

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:13.400
On the other hand,
Competitor Dande has only lost one,

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:16.070
leaving him
with five Pokémon to use.

00:13:16.070 --> 00:13:18.190
Numelgon! Great Blaze!

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:25.830
It’s super effective!

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:30.330
Gorillander’s eliminated
Competitor Carne’s Pokémon one after another!

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:34.340
Will this powerful Fire move
finally take it down?!

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:49.600
And Gorillander holds on!

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:51.230
Impossible!

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:52.940
Acrobatics!

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:07.330
Numelgon is unable to battle!

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:14.210
All right! Good work!
One more and you’re in the finals!

00:14:14.210 --> 00:14:15.670
He’s so cool!

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:17.460
Gorillander’s so strong!

00:14:18.340 --> 00:14:20.960
I’ve never seen Ms. Carne
so overpowered...

00:14:25.390 --> 00:14:28.850
It looks like in the end
you’re all I have left.

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:32.600
You’re on, Sirknight!

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:42.570
Everyone!
Have you been watching?

00:14:42.570 --> 00:14:48.330
This is match one of the
Pokémon World Championships semifinals!

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:53.370
In the battle between Competitor Dande, Galar’s Champion;
and Competitor Carne, Kalos’s Champion...

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:02.880
Competitor Dande’s frenzied attacks have taken down
Competitor Carne’s Pokémon one after another, meow!

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:07.510
After this and that, her last Pokémon
is everyone’s favorite, Sirknight!

00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:13.850
Princess Number 28,
what are your impressions on the battle so far?

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:18.650
Pumpjin lost,
so who cares anymore?

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:22.400
It’s not over till the dust settles!

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:25.240
After all, she’s a star actress!

00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:28.870
We’re cheering for
Competitor Carne, meow!

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:32.790
Shadow Ball!

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:36.330
Knock Off!

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:46.470
Psychokinesis!

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:02.320
Gorillander is unable to battle!

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:07.820
Gorillander finally goes down!
Competitor Carne’s counterattack has begun!

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:13.120
You fought well.

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:15.830
Come out, Lizardon!

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:22.340
Lizardon...

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:27.340
Competitor Dande’s ace,
Lizardon, has arrived!

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:30.180
Let’s finish this, Lizardon!

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:33.720
En garde, Dande!

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:37.140
Sirknight! Mega Evolve!

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:11.470
So you’re using Mega Evolution...

00:17:11.470 --> 00:17:14.720
That means...
it’s Champion time!

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:17.220
All right! This is it!

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:30.200
Kyodai... max!

00:17:39.790 --> 00:17:42.790
It’s Kyodaimax Lizardon!

00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:44.380
100,000 Volts!

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:50.630
Now that’s powerful!

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:57.260
Whoa! Kyodaimax Lizardon
was greatly shaken!

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:05.020
Kyodai Hellfire!

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:21.370
Whoa! Incredible flames
wrap around Mega Sirknight!

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:24.120
Psychokinesis!

00:18:38.140 --> 00:18:39.140
What?!

00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:40.720
Is this real?!

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:44.520
Incredible! It’s controlling the flames
with Psychokinesis!

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:46.810
That’s pretty good!

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:49.150
Lizardon! Dai Jet!

00:19:12.300 --> 00:19:14.300
What’s going on?!

00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:17.680
The Psychokinesis,
the Kyodai Hellfire, and the Dai Jet...

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:19.550
They’ve all combined into one!

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:25.810
Ms. Carne and Sirknight’s desire to never give up
is giving them strength.

00:19:26.440 --> 00:19:27.440
Sirknight!

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:36.660
Lizardon!
One more Kyodai Hellfire!

00:19:36.660 --> 00:19:38.570
Blow them away!

00:19:45.290 --> 00:19:50.170
An incredible blast
swallows Mega Sirknight!

00:20:05.020 --> 00:20:07.190
Sirknight is unable to battle!

00:20:07.190 --> 00:20:10.810
As such, the winner is...
Competitor Dande!

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:16.700
It’s over!
Competitor Dande heads into the finals!

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:27.160
<i>Woo!</i>
Big bro, you’re the best!

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:29.420
Wow... Amazing!

00:20:29.420 --> 00:20:31.250
Lizardon’s so strong!

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:33.710
Yeah! It’s <i>unbelievable!</i>

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:37.090
I wanna have cool battles
just like Mr. Dande!

00:20:37.470 --> 00:20:42.350
You’ll need to adventure lots,
catch lots, and battle lots to do that.

00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:46.850
Yeah! When I get my partner,
can I battle you two?!

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:47.850
I wanna, too!

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:49.940
Yeah, let’s do it!

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:53.980
You’ve got yourself
some new little rivals.

00:20:54.610 --> 00:20:55.780
Thank you.

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:05.950
Congratulations on
reaching the finals.

00:21:07.790 --> 00:21:10.170
You made me sweat
time and time again.

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:13.130
I was just lucky today, that’s all.

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:22.890
So Mr. Dande will be waiting
in the finals...

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:34.440
Satoshi and Shirona are finally about to clash
over a spot in the finals match against Dande.

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:36.190
Who will win?

00:23:06.450 --> 00:23:10.910
<i>Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament News!</i>

00:23:11.450 --> 00:23:13.290
The second semifinals
match will be...

00:23:13.290 --> 00:23:16.040
...Competitor Shirona versus
Competitor Brat Boy, meow!

00:23:16.040 --> 00:23:18.920
Wait... She sent out
a pretty creepy Pokémon, meow...

00:23:18.920 --> 00:23:20.300
It looks pretty strong!

00:23:20.300 --> 00:23:23.210
That pansy’s nothing special!
Bleh, I say! Bleh!

00:23:23.210 --> 00:23:24.720
Uh, it’s looking this way, meow.

00:23:24.720 --> 00:23:26.090
It’s coming!

00:23:26.470 --> 00:23:28.850
H-H-Hey, wait!

00:23:28.850 --> 00:23:30.350
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.350 --> 00:23:32.310
The Semifinals II: Bedazzle

00:23:32.310 --> 00:23:34.140
Let’s all tune in, meow!
